    "result_text": "The full test suite passed (`AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class; the other two files are the shared base and a support helper). \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, returning **400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `ValidateRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a small validation function (single responsibility) that reads the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws only when a date is *present* and after `LocalDate.now()`. It judges the raw supplied date, before `ResolveRegistrationDate` rolls it onto a business day.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a checked exception carrying the offending date, modeled on the existing `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with the message, mirroring the existing handlers.\n- Escalation YAML mapping the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:** added a `validateRegistrationDate` step to `owners.POST.yml`, placed right after `validate` (field-presence) so a well-formed request's date is checked early, before postcode/telephone rules \u2014 and crucially before `build`/`resolveRegistrationDate`, so the check sees the value exactly as supplied.\n\nThis reuses the established validate-step + checked-exception + escalation-handler pattern rather than bolting the logic onto `ResolveRegistrationDate`, keeping each unit focused.",
